"Captar-Libras Dataset | VeRLab (https://verlab.github.io/captar-libras/)\nciteturn35view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn33view3\",\"id\":15}); Total lines: 127\nL0: 【0†Image: VeRLab Logo】\nL1: # Captar-Libras\nL2: \nL3: A Unified Multimodal Dataset for Brazilian Sign Language Tasks\nL4: 【1†Cauã Magalhães†github.com】^{1}, 【2†Bruno Lages†www.linkedin.com】^{1}, 【3†Ari Filho†www.linkedin.com】^{1}, 【4†Jéssica Ramos†www.linkedin.com】,\nL5: 【5†Paulo de Souza Coelho†www.linkedin.com】, 【6†Michel Silva†michelmelosilva.github.io】^{2}, 【7†Thiago L. Gomes†www2.dpi.ufv.br】^{2},\nL6: 【8†Milena Soriano Marcolino†scholar.google.com.br】^{2}, 【9†Elidéa Bernardino†www.letras.ufmg.br】^{2}, 【10†Raquel O. Prates†dcc.ufmg.br】^{1},\nL7: 【11†Mario F. M. Campos†dcc.ufmg.br】^{1}, 【12†Erickson R. Nascimento†dcc.ufmg.br】^{1}\nL8: ^{1}【13†Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais (UFMG)†www.ufmg.br】\nL9: ^{2}【14†Universidade Federal de Viçosa (UFV)†www.ufv.br】\nL10: \nL11: 【15†Read Paper】 【16†View Repo†github.com】 【17†Dataset Part 1†huggingface.co】 【18†Dataset Part 2†huggingface.co】\nL12: \nL13: ⚠️ Important: Our dataset requires credentialized access. The datasets on HuggingFace are gated and access must be authorized after you agree to the terms and conditions. Please visit the dataset repositories and request access through HuggingFace.\nL14: ## Dataset Overview\nL15: \nL16: Captar-Libras is a large-scale multimodal dataset for Brazilian Sign Language (Libras), comprising video sequences from native Deaf signers performing sentences in the medical domain. Data was collected in a controlled capture environment using four synchronized cameras: a frontal RGB-D camera, two wide-angle cameras covering lateral and zenithal views, and a dedicated high-definition facial camera. This enables rich spatial and temporal modeling of body, hand, and facial expressions.\nL17: Each recording follows a guided protocol to ensure linguistic consistency and is annotated with frame-level gloss temporal alignments produced by specialist annotators. The dataset includes raw multi-view recordings, preprocessed video segments, structured gloss and text annotations, and precomputed full-body pose sequences in SMPL-X format. A signer-independent train/validation/test split stratified by gender and skin tone is provided as the recommended evaluation protocol.\nL18: ### Key Statistics\nL19: \nL20: ### Over 24,000\nL21: \nL22: Video Sequences\nL23: \nL24: ### 78\nL25: \nL26: Signers (50F / 28M)\nL27: \nL28: ### 375\nL29: \nL30: Sentences\nL31: \nL32: ### 4\nL33: \nL34: Camera Views\nL35: \nL36: ## Data Access\nL37: \nL38: ### Annotations\nL39: \nL40: Structured gloss and text annotations for all sequences in the dataset.\nL41: \nL42: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL43: \nL44: Copy\nL45: \nL46:     ``\nL47: \nL48: ### Frontal RGB\nL49: \nL50: High-resolution frontal RGB video streams from the frontal camera.\nL51: \nL52: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL53: \nL54: Copy\nL55: \nL56:     ``\nL57: ### Frontal Depth\nL58: \nL59: Depth sequences from the frontal RGB-D camera for 3D reconstruction.\nL60: \nL61: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL62: \nL63: Copy\nL64: \nL65:     ``\nL66: \nL67: ### Lateral View\nL68: \nL69: Wide-angle camera covering lateral perspective (side view).\nL70: \nL71: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL72: \nL73: Copy\nL74: \nL75:     ``\nL76: \nL77: ### Zenithal View\nL78: \nL79: Wide-angle camera covering zenithal perspective (top-down view).\nL80: \nL81: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL82: \nL83: Copy\nL84: \nL85:     ``\nL86: ### Facial HD\nL87: \nL88: Dedicated high-definition facial camera for fine-grained facial expression analysis.\nL89: \nL90: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL91: \nL92: Copy\nL93: \nL94:     ``\nL95: \nL96: ### SMPL-X Poses\nL97: \nL98: Precomputed full-body 3D pose sequences in SMPL-X format for all sequences.\nL99: \nL100: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL101: \nL102: Copy\nL103: \nL104:     ``\nL105: \nL106: ### Preprocessed Videos\nL107: \nL108: Preprocessed video segments used in the baseline experiments.\nL109: \nL110: 【15†Show Download Snippet】\nL111: \nL112: Copy\nL113: \nL114:     ``\nL115: ## Citation\nL116: If you use Captar-Libras in your research, please cite it using the following BibTeX entry:\nL117: \nL118:     `@inproceedings{magalhaes2026captarlibras,\nL119:                     title={Captar-Libras: A Unified Multimodal Dataset for Brazilian Sign Language Tasks},\nL120:                     author={Cauã Magalhães and Bruno Lages and Ari Filho and Jéssica Ramos and Paulo de Souza Coelho and Michel Silva and Thiago L. Gomes and Milena Soriano Marcolino and Elidéa Bernardino and Raquel O. Prates and Mario F. M. Campos and Erickson R. Nascimento},\nL121:                     year={2026},\nL122:                     booktitle={The Fortieth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems Evaluations and Datasets Track}\nL123:                 }`\nL124: Copy\nL125: \nL126: © 2026 VeRLab - UFMG | Computer Vision and Robotics Lab\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLSWH100 - Libras SignWriting Handshape | Zenodo (https://zenodo.org/records/10635628)\nciteturn35view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn33view1\",\"pattern\":\"License\"}); Total lines: 185\nL0: Published June 3, 2024 | Version 1\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Dataset】 Open\nL3: \nL4: # LSWH100 - Libras SignWriting Handshape\nL5: \nL6: ### Authors/Creators\nL7: \nL8:   * 【1†Coelho Lobo-Neto, Vicente (Researcher)^{1}】\nL9: \nL10: [Button: Show affiliations ]\nL11: \nL12:   * 1. Universidade Estadual de Campinas (UNICAMP)\nL13: \nL14: ### Contributors\nL15: \nL16: ### Supervisor:\nL17: \nL18:   * 【2†Pedrini, Helio^{1}】\nL19: \nL20: [Button: Show affiliations ]\nL21: \nL22:   * 1. Universidade Estadual de Campinas (UNICAMP)\nL23: ## Description\nL24: Libras SignWriting Handshape (LSWH100) is a new handshape dataset focused on Sign Language Recognition. The dataset includes 144,000 synthetic images of a realistic human hand, covering 100 distinct handshape classes used in Brazillian Sign Language (Libras). Each handshape is represented from four different perspectives: front, back, left and right. However, the perspectives are independent of each other.\nL25: In other words, the hands represented in one perspective will not be the same as those in other perspectives. Handshapes are named using the convention from SignWriting, a writing system for sign languages. The dataset contains annotations for classification, detection, segmentation, depth estimation, and 3D hand keypoints. Images include indoor and outdoor scenes during different times of day, centered on a single hand that can change size, 3D rotation, and skin tone.\nL26: We generated these images using Blender, a free and open-source 3D creation software.\nL27: ## Files\nL28: \nL29: ###\nL30: \nL31: back.zip\nL32: \nL33: 【3†Preview】\nL34: ###\nL35: \nL36: Files (17.7 GB)\nL37: Name  | Size  |\nL38: --- | --- | ---\nL39: 【4†back.zip】 md5:dd64afc5e66ef379bac803283fe9edd7  | 4.4 GB  | 【3†Preview】 【4†Download】\nL40: 【5†class_list.csv】 md5:64a84d39a985136d5b75ef333328a1ce  | 2.8 kB  | 【6†Preview】 【5†Download】\nL41: 【7†class_list_with_images.pdf】 md5:0a827ae24019d34dbe8f515d09a6fb84  | 8.6 MB  | 【8†Preview】 【7†Download】\nL42: 【9†front.zip】 md5:8a7e51f41e43b418b4a36973ce045e14  | 4.5 GB  | 【10†Preview】 【9†Download】\nL43: 【11†left.zip】 md5:2a09cebbdbd239d158f793282a144d86  | 4.3 GB  | 【12†Preview】 【11†Download】\nL44: 【13†right.zip】 md5:a289a32385e46532dc817ab946835915  | 4.4 GB  | 【14†Preview】 【13†Download】\nL45: 【15†test_annotations.coco.json】 md5:5a7a44a526c955b61f9a9bdf4581a8e3  | 11.7 MB  | 【16†Preview】 【15†Download】\nL46: 【17†train_annotations.coco.json】 md5:15211578a754cfa3024a99b7765d283e  | 116.7 MB  | 【18†Preview】 【17†Download】\nL47: 【19†val_annotations.coco.json】 md5:9fe7075360776c27cb6ec3d5aca5297f  | 11.7 MB  | 【